@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Host shell → Go: retire every bash script the operator's Mac executes
' purpose: remove macOS /bin/bash 3.2 from every host code path
' would touch: defs/lib/docker-build.sh, defs/*/build.sh, defs/*/ensure.sh (deleted)
' would touch: defs/*/test.sh, defs/*/tests/*.sh (harness deleted; in-image command strings kept)
' would touch: lib/*.sh, scripts/*.sh, mise.toml
' would touch: internal/maintain/** (BuildPlan, DeployPlan, TestPlan), cmd/proveo/provision.go
' would touch: internal/imagebuild/targets.go (the build table; P2 put it here, not in harness.manifest)
' would touch: internal/contract/{agent_pin,image_resolution,host_bash}_test.go (buildx_pull_policy deleted in P2)
' session: 92196ee8-2438-4fda-ac25-7311bf16c563
' PLANNED 2026-09-22. P1 and P2 LANDED 2026-09-22; P3 and P4 open.
' Decided by the operator over fish (no errexit, non-POSIX at every
' Kit/sbx/Dockerfile/installer boundary) and over a mise-pinned bash 5
' (provision.go ran `bash build.sh` for END USERS, who get 3.2, until P2).
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── MEASURED 2026-09-22, BEFORE P2: WHERE THE SHELL RAN ───────────────────
'   host build   defs/lib + build.sh + ensure.sh   ~1.2k lines   macOS 3.2
'   host libs    lib/*.sh + scripts/*.sh           ~0.6k lines   macOS 3.2
'   def tests    defs/*/tests/*.sh HARNESS         ~3.3k lines   macOS 3.2
'   in-image     packages/lib + entrypoints        ~3.8k lines   Debian bash 5
'   installer    apps/cli/public/cli/install.sh                  any POSIX sh
' The def tests were first filed as in-container; they are not. helpers.sh
' sourced docker-build.sh (now the slim defs/lib/test-image.sh), falls back
' when `timeout` is missing, and drives `docker run … bash -c "<cmd>"` FROM the
' host. Only <cmd> runs inside.
' End users reached host bash too: cmd/proveo/provision.go ran
' `bash <def>/build.sh` when an image was missing. P2 removed that path.
'
' ── WHAT STAYS SHELL, AND WHY ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' In-image bash: it only ever meets bash 5, and sbx Kit startup commands, `sbx
' exec … bash -c` (internal/sbx/run.go) and Dockerfile RUN lines speak it.
' The installer: `curl | sh` on a machine that has no proveo yet, so POSIX sh.
' The <cmd> strings inside def tests: they execute in the image, not the host.
'
' ── PHASES (each one ships green and deletes what it replaces) ─────────────
' P1  internal/imagebuild — the docker-build.sh primitives in Go: agent version
'     pin (npm / pypi / github), image ref + resolve + require-published, buildx
'     builder ensure + driver choice, pull policy, cache flags, registry-DNS
'     help, browser variant. The contract tables that exec those shell
'     functions are ported as Go unit tests; the shell tests STAY until P2
'     deletes the shell, because build.sh still runs it. Image resolution
'     already lives in Go (internal/maintain.ResolveImage).
'     LANDED 2026-09-22 as internal/imagebuild. Deliberate differences:
'       * `-t repo` with no tag is `:latest` and refused for --load; the
'         shell's `${a##*:}` returned the whole ref and let it through.
'       * npm reads the registry JSON (NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY honoured) rather
'         than `npm view`; pypi needs no python3 fallback.
'       * output goes through internal/ui (Notef/Warnf/Failf), not emoji.
' P2  declarative build — each def's variants, Dockerfile, base, build-args and
'     parent chain move into a `build:` block in harness.manifest.
'     maintain.BuildPlan / DeployPlan and provision.go call imagebuild directly.
'     PARITY GATE before deletion: for every target and variant, the buildx
'     argv Go renders equals the argv the old script ran (golden, --print).
'     Then build.sh, ensure.sh and docker-build.sh are deleted.
'     LANDED 2026-09-22. Every defs/*/build.sh, defs/*/ensure.sh and
'     defs/lib/docker-build.sh is deleted.
'       * DEVIATION: the recipes live in a Go table, internal/imagebuild/
'         targets.go `Specs` (Repo, Override, Dockerfile, Context, Parent,
'         Needs, Layer, Pins, EnvArgs, Floor), not in a harness.manifest
'         `build:` block. 6 of the 16 registry targets (the four bases, the
'         two sidecars) have no manifest to hold one, and
'         TestEverySpecIsARegistryTarget pins the table to maintain.Registry.
'       * ensure = push → RequirePublished; present + Floor ok → done;
'         present without Floor → rebuild; absent → pull, else build. Each
'         Floor is the in-image `sh -c` probe its ensure.sh used to run.
'       * PARITY: internal/imagebuild/parity_test.go + testdata/
'         build_argv.golden, 48 cases (16 targets x --load, --push, cold
'         host; 83 buildx invocations), written
'         while build.sh and BuildTarget rendered identical buildx argv.
'       * maintain: Target.BuildScript/BuildArgs gone, Target.RepoRoot added;
'         BuildPlan/DeployPlan emit `imagebuild <target> --tag T [--push]
'         [--no-cache]` as an in-process Command.Run step.
'       * BUG FIXED (provision.go): the end-user fallback ran `bash build.sh`
'         with no args, which defaulted to :latest and was refused for --load.
'         It now builds the image's target at :local when asked for :latest
'         (buildTag) and hands the run that ref; PreflightImages returns the
'         image it settled on.
'       * PROVEO_<X>_IMAGE names the target's repo; --tag sets the tag.
'       * FINDING: codex is NOT pinned. CODEX_VERSION is an EnvArg defaulting
'         to `latest`, exactly as its build.sh did; parity kept it, and
'         agent_pin_test does not cover codex. Recorded in
'         _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml.
'       * The def tests keep a slim defs/lib/test-image.sh (proveo_ref_tag,
'         proveo_image_created, proveo_resolve_image, proveo_test_image)
'         until P3.
' P3  def tests → Go — the TOOLS/CONFIG arrays are already tables; they become
'     `-tags=image` table tests. A context deadline replaces `timeout`/
'     `gtimeout`. test.sh and tests/*.sh are deleted; TestPlan runs go test.
' P4  lib/ + scripts/ — ui/registry/helpers callers and go-test-coverage.sh /
'     stage-cli-cdn.sh become Go (subcommands or `go run` mise tasks).
'
' ── THE GATE THAT FINISHES IT ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' TestHostScriptsAvoidBash4Builtins shrinks with each phase. After P4 it is
' replaced by: no tracked *.sh outside packages/lib, defs/*/entrypoint.sh
' (in-image) and apps/cli/public/cli (installer).

rectangle "operator's Mac" as MAC <<host>> {
  component "proveo build / provision\nexec bash build.sh — BEFORE P2" as NOW <<error>>
  component "internal/imagebuild\nGo — LANDED P2" as GO <<app>>
  component "go test -tags=image\ndef tests — AFTER P3" as GT <<app>>
}
rectangle "image (Debian)" as IMG <<host>> {
  component "packages/lib + entrypoints\nbash 5 — stays" as INIMG <<app>>
}
component "install.sh\nPOSIX sh — stays" as INST <<app>>

NOW ARROW_ERROR GO : replaced, parity-gated
GO ARROW_MAIN IMG : docker buildx
GT ARROW_MAIN IMG : docker run <cmd>
INST ARROW_MAIN MAC : bootstraps proveo

note right of NOW
  **End users hit this path.**
  provision.go ran `bash build.sh`
  on a missing image, so a fix for
  contributors alone left them on 3.2.
end note

note bottom of GO
  **Parity before deletion.**
  48 golden cases matched each old
  build.sh argv, per target and
  mode, before the scripts went.
end note

note bottom of GT
  **The arrays are already tables.**
  TOOLS / CONFIG entries map 1:1
  to Go table rows; a context
  deadline replaces the missing
  macOS `timeout` binary.
end note

note right of INIMG
  **Never meets 3.2.**
  Kit startup, `sbx exec bash -c`
  and Dockerfile RUN speak it, so
  moving it would add a boundary
  instead of removing one.
end note

note right of INST
  **Runs before proveo exists.**
  `curl | sh` on a stranger's box:
  POSIX sh is the only interpreter
  guaranteed to be there, so it
  stays shell by necessity.
end note
@enduml
